From 21e4e50364c421ef001519e1b21623f77fc3b34b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:37:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material: component by component layout of the arrays

The constructors of `Material` and `MaterialArrays` take the layout of
the arrays (point by point by default, or component by component, which
gives coalesced accesses on a GPU), given to the material data manager
of MGIS. The deformation gradients are initialized to the identity in
both layouts.

The accessors based on a stride between points (`getGradient`,
`getThermodynamicForce`, `getInternalStateVariable`) refuse the
component by component layout with a message; the accessors of the
energies (one component, same array in both layouts) accept both. The
behaviour integrators keep the point by point layout.

MaterialArraysTest: every check in both layouts, layout given to MGIS,
identity of the deformation gradients read through the views of MGIS
(fails if the layout is ignored), accessors refused in the component by
component layout.
---
 include/MFEMMGIS/Material.hxx       |  8 +++++-
 include/MFEMMGIS/MaterialArrays.hxx | 11 ++++++--
 src/Material.cxx                    | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/MaterialArrays.cxx              | 18 ++++++++----
 tests/MaterialArraysTest.cxx        | 35 +++++++++++++++++------
 5 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

